{
  "opening": "This release introduces several new functions and refactors existing ones to improve usability and consistency. It also updates type checking logic and removes legacy Python 2 support, ensuring the library remains modern and robust.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m01",
      "text": "The public API must expose a function named 'apply' that accepts an iterable of arguments and applies them to a callable. Additionally, 'identity' and 'thread_first' must remain available as standard utility functions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "The module must provide 'compose_left' and 'pipe' functions for building data processing pipelines. These should allow chaining functions where the output of one serves as input to the next, with 'pipe' supporting variable argument counts."
    },
    {
      "id": "m03",
      "text": "A new function named 'peekn' must be exposed, which yields items from an iterator while storing up to n items in memory for later access. The existing 'peek' function should continue to operate as before for single-item inspection."
    },
    {
      "id": "m07",
      "text": "The 'fold' function must support parallel execution by accepting a worker function and distributing tasks across multiple processes. Its signature and return behavior should remain consistent with previous versions while enabling multiprocessing capabilities."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09",
      "text": "The breakpoint-related functionality must maintain its current signature and behavior, ensuring compatibility with debugging tools. No changes to the public interface are required beyond preserving existing error handling and output formats."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14",
      "text": "The 'merge' and 'merge_with' functions must accept any Mapping type rather than strictly requiring dict instances. This allows broader compatibility with custom mapping implementations while preserving the original merging logic and output format."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "All listed functions including 'curry', 'Compose', 'excepts', and others must be fully compatible with Python 3 only, removing any Python 2-specific code paths. The 'curried' name must be explicitly exposed as a public alias or submodule for backward compatibility."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31",
      "text": "Warning messages generated by the library must be improved for clarity and actionable feedback, particularly when configuration issues arise. The 'get_config_from_root' function should continue to return configuration values without altering its core behavior."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public names are correctly exported and documented. Verify that no internal implementation details leak into the public API surface."
}
